  "limitations": [
    "API-09 still owns the process-wide application/problem+json vocabulary, shared correlation middleware, browser Origin, CSRF and Fetch-Metadata enforcement, trusted proxy policy, and global timeout and retry controls. API-06 supplies route-local JSON-only mutations, fixed safe errors, private response headers, and server-generated correlation IDs but does not claim that larger boundary.",
    "Normal planning creates generation-one requests atomically with the complete authorization set. The explicit route therefore treats generation zero as ensure/replay and fails closed when that initial complete set is absent; it never inserts one isolated approval leaf. Positive generations are expiry-only renewals of the unchanged action and set epoch.",
    "The authenticated renewal winner becomes the replacement generation's immutable requester and audit actor, so a no-self-approval policy applies to that generation's creator. First-generation planner requester provenance remains a pre-existing intake and planning-boundary concern.",
    "DEL-04 owns Alembic migrations and upgrade/bootstrap behavior. API-06 adds the bounded optional decision-reason ORM field and proves metadata-created SQLite persistence and keyed-integrity validation, but does not claim a migration or live PostgreSQL DDL/runtime execution; the optional PostgreSQL portability test may skip when its driver is absent.",
    "DEL-05 owns default runnable service composition. The routes are installed and fail closed without complete asynchronous executors; API-06 integration injects the real decision/resource services and durable unit of work rather than claiming the default process constructs them.",
    "API-07 owns the run, step, action, template, and instance detail resources referenced by returned links. API-06 returns stable reserved URLs but does not claim those target resources are implemented yet.",
    "The decision service retains RUN-10's isolated-fixture allowance for a parent Run in received state. Normal persisted write plans enter awaiting_approval before public decisions; API-06 does not claim that the legacy received-state allowance is a substitute for composed workflow sequencing."
  ]
